<title>UK: INTERVIEW-Tarmac private sector drives growth.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW-Tarmac private sector drives growth.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tarmac Plc, the UK building group, said on Thursday that commercial building, projects for the Millennium and the private finance initiative (PFI) would all help drive results further ahead this year.</p>
<p>Neville Simms, chief executive, told Reuters in an interview, &quot;Government spending will remain subdued even if we do have a new administration. But commercial building is up strongly and housing, the Millennium and PFI should all help fill the gap.&quot;</p>
</text>
